    <item>
      <title>Small Talk</title>
      <link>http://127.0.0.1:1313/stories/small-talk/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 24 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://127.0.0.1:1313/stories/small-talk/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;i-first&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;I.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It was a sticky Thursday. The afternoon air wrapped around and between the leaves and the boys watched cars grind north on Third Avenue.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;ii-next&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;II.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Next&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Steve tapped his black shoes together. &amp;ldquo;I&amp;rsquo;m hungry.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;Yeah, it was a lousy lunch. Those sandwiches were like the ones from soccer.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Steve nodded.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;I&amp;rsquo;ll make you something tonight, maybe tortellini.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Steve smiled and closed his eyes. &amp;ldquo;So where&amp;rsquo;s Mom now?&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Elliott shook his head. &amp;ldquo;I don&amp;rsquo;t know.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
